{title: Numerals Test}
{artist: setDING}
{key: C}

{start_of_verse: label="Major: the seven degrees"}
[C]One and [Dm]two and [Em]three and [F]four
[G]Five and [Am]six, [Bdim]seven, [C]home once more
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: label="Jazz: ii – V – I"}
[Dm7]Quiet [G7]steps back [Cmaj7]home
[Em7]Lights up[A7]on the [Dm9]wall
[G13]Late at [C6/9]night
[Am(maj7)]Shadows [Am7]in the [D7]hall
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: label="Borrowed chords"}
[C]Then a [Bb7]detour, [Eb]far and [Ab]wide
[Db]Naples [G7b9]calls, it's [G7#11]time to [C]ride
[Caug]Tension, [Csus4]floating, [C]rest
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_bridge: label="Bass notes and secondary dominants"}
[C/E]Up the [F]stairs, [G/B]one more [C]flight
[C/Bb]Down a[F/A]gain, step [Fm/Ab]by step, [G7]right
[E7]Dominant [Am]of the six
[D7]Dominant [G7]of the five
{end_of_bridge}

{key: Am}
{start_of_verse: label="Minor in A (jazz style)"}
[Am]Minor [Bm7b5]starts, [E7]dominant [Am]bright
[Dm7]On the [G]way back [C]home to[F]night
[Bdim7]Degree [E7b9]seven, [Am]end
{end_of_verse}
